course: dictionary
lesson: 13774
title: The interviewee
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An interview has two people. One person asks the questions, and the other person answers them. The person who answers is the interviewee. Many words ending in -ee name the person who receives an action, so the interviewee is the person being interviewed.
explain: «Mrs Patel was the interviewee, and she answered every question about her job as a nurse.» The clue is answered every question: she is the one replying. Check by swapping in the meaning: the person who answers the questions was Mrs Patel. It still makes sense.
explain: Interviewees are not only for jobs. «In our science project, Sam asked his neighbours about recycling, and each one was an interviewee.» In a survey or research study, the interviewee is the person who gives the answers.
fact: Interviewee means the person who answers the questions in an interview.
fact: The person who asks the questions is the interviewer, so the two words are partners.
fact: «Interviewee» can mean a job applicant, a school place applicant, or someone speaking to a newspaper or TV programme.
fact: In a survey or research study, an interviewee is a person who answers the questions.
fact: «Interviewees» is the plural: more than one person being interviewed.
exercise: «The interviewee sat up straight and smiled at the panel.» What is the interviewee? | The room where the interview takes place | *The person who answers the questions | The job being offered | The person who asks the questions
exercise: «The interviewer asked the first question, and the interviewee took a deep breath.» Find and copy the word that means the person who answers. | breath | interviewer | question | *interviewee
exercise: In Sam's history project, Grandad talked about his childhood. Who was the interviewee? | *Grandad | Sam | The class | The teacher
test: «Nadia felt nervous, but the interviewer made her feel at ease.» In this sentence, who is the interviewee? | The head teacher | The school | *Nadia | The interviewer
test: In a research study, who gives the answers to the questions? | *The interviewee | The printer of the questionnaire | The person who counts the results | The researcher who writes the study
exam: Which word means a person who is asked questions on a TV programme? | Audience | Viewer | Interviewer | *Interviewee
